# Adlaire Editor Master Specification

`Docs/Editor_Master_Spec` is the source of truth for the structured editor runtime and WYSIWYG Editor UI details.

## Scope

| Area | Managed by |
| --- | --- |
| Editor runtime source | `TypeScript/Editor/` |
| Editor runtime output | `EditorUI/editor.js` |
| WYSIWYG Editor UI source | `TypeScript/EditorUI/wysiwyg.ts` |
| WYSIWYG Editor UI output | `EditorUI/wysiwyg.css`, `EditorUI/wysiwyg.js` |
| WYSIWYG UI catalog | `Docs/WYSIWYG_Editor_UI_Catalog` |

## Runtime Modules

| Module | Responsibility |
| --- | --- |
| `core.ts` | Editor creation and runtime coordination. |
| `document.ts` | Structured document data and block operations. |
| `commands.ts` | Command definitions and command execution. |
| `selection.ts` | Selection model. |
| `history.ts` | Undo and redo history. |
| `validation.ts` | Document, command, and selection validation. |
| `events.ts` | Runtime events. |
| `types.ts` | Shared editor types. |
| `index.ts` | Public TypeScript entry point. |

The runtime keeps invalid commands from mutating document state. Duplicate block identifiers, invalid payloads, and invalid selection references are errors.

## Runtime Contract

| Contract | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| Public entry point | `TypeScript/Editor/index.ts` exports the runtime modules and the `AdlaireEditor` browser global. |
| Command boundary | `commands.ts` owns command execution and returns non-mutating failures for invalid commands. |
| Document boundary | `document.ts` owns block creation, registries, normalization, paste handling, and block lookup helpers. |
| Selection boundary | `selection.ts` owns selection position helpers and must not mutate documents. |
| History boundary | `history.ts` owns undo/redo state and keeps document snapshots isolated. |
| Validation boundary | `validation.ts` owns document, block, command, and selection validation. |
| Event boundary | `events.ts` owns editor event and error construction. |
| Type boundary | `types.ts` owns shared runtime types and does not import implementation modules. |
| Output boundary | `EditorUI/editor.js` is generated runtime output and is checked for the public browser global. |

## UI Surface

WYSIWYG Editor UI covers:

- editor shell
- toolbar
- inline toolbar
- block selection
- block insertion
- transformation
- drag and reorder affordances
- mobile toolbar and bottom sheet
- readonly, disabled, locked, warning, and error states
- publication and accessibility support surfaces

Concrete class coverage is maintained in `Docs/WYSIWYG_Editor_UI_Catalog`.

## Boundaries

- Generic public UI belongs in `Docs/Generic_Component_Catalog`.
- Admin UI belongs in `Docs/Admin_UI_Catalog`.
- Editor runtime internals belong in this file and `TypeScript/Editor/`.
- Samples may demonstrate editor UI, but Samples are not the source of truth.

## Checks

The repository check verifies required files, generated outputs, catalog governance terms, editor runtime exports, module boundaries, and forbidden dependency patterns.
